data: {"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"data\": {\n    \"lookupStatus\": \"found\",\n    \"posts\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"3750981788388435\",\n        \"url\": \"https://www.facebook.com/groups/862950587191584/permalink/3750981788388435/\",\n        \"text\": \"Now just imagine the NAIA decided to change their soccer into the two-semester season...\",\n        \"publishedAt\": \"2026-11-06T11:13:14.000Z\",\n        \"reactionCount\": 1,\n        \"commentCount\": 2,\n        \"isPaidPartnership\": null,\n        \"sharedPostId\": null,\n        \"sharedPostUrl\": null,\n        \"author\": {\n          \"id\": \"200300067\",\n          \"name\": \"Chris Cousins\",\n          \"url\": null\n        },\n        \"video\": {\n          \"thumbnailUrl\": null,\n          \"durationMs\": null,\n          \"sdUrl\": null,\n          \"hdUrl\": null\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"3750963885056892\",\n        \"url\": \"https://www.facebook.com/groups/862950587191584/permalink/3750963885056892/\",\n        \"text\": \"⚽ **NCAA men’s soccer two-semester model: the numbers behind the debate**\\n\\nCollege Soccer HQ’s latest public count reports **241 votes to overturn the proposal**, reaching the required threshold.\\n\\nHere’s the breakdown:\\n\\n▪️ **140** came from institutions with men’s soccer.\\n▪️ **101** came from institutions without men’s soccer.\\n▪️ **58%** of the reported rescission votes therefore came from schools that sponsor the sport.\\n▪️ **28 institutions** are listed as publicly backing the model.\\n\\nThe reported rescission count rose from **183 on November 2 to 241 on November 5**, an increase of 58.\\n\\nSupporters highlight recovery time, player development and reduced midweek travel. Those seeking rescission raise concerns about staffing, costs, facilities, weather and the impact on other sports.\\n\\nInstitutional positions do not necessarily reflect the views of every coach or player. Schools without a reported position should not automatically be counted as supporting either side.\\n\\nThese figures reflect public reporting, rather than an official final NCAA tally. The page states that votes can be withdrawn until voting closes on November 6 at 5pm ET.\\n\\n🔎 Explore the full breakdown and search by school or conference:\\n\\n[https://collegesoccerhq.com/resources/two-semester-model](https://collegesoccerhq.com/resources/two-semester-model)\\n\\n#CollegeSoccer #NCAASoccer #SRUSA\",\n        \"publishedAt\": \"2026-11-06T10:55:29.000Z\",\n        \"reactionCount\": 7,\n        \"commentCount\": 4,\n        \"isPaidPartnership\": null,\n        \"sharedPostId\": null,\n        \"sharedPostUrl\": null,\n        \"author\": {\n          \"id\": \"200300067\",\n          \"name\": \"Chris Cousins\",\n          \"url\": null\n        },\n        \"video\": {\n          \"thumbnailUrl\": null,\n          \"durationMs\": null,\n          \"sdUrl\": null,\n          \"hdUrl\": null\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"3750768275076453\",\n        \"url\": \"https://www.facebook.com/groups/862950587191584/permalink/3750768275076453/\",\n        \"text\": \"🚨 𝐓𝐖𝐎-𝐒𝐄𝐌𝐄𝐒𝐓𝐄𝐑 𝐌𝐎𝐃𝐄𝐋 𝐔𝐏𝐃𝐀𝐓𝐄\\n\\n📋 Reports suggest the #NCAA Division I two-semester model for men’s soccer is set to be rescinded. #SRUSA understands that the 241 votes needed have now been reached, and sources indicate the proposal is unlikely to survive.\\n\\n⚠️ The result has not been officially confirmed, and voting closes today at 5pm ET.\\n\\n➡️ What this means if the reports are correct:\\n\\n▪️ The proposal is defeated and Division I men’s soccer stays on its current fall calendar\\n\\n▪️ The year-round model would not take effect in 2027-28\\n\\n▪️ The Cabinet affirmed the proposal on 7th October, but it fell short of the 75 percent needed to avoid the rescission period\\n\\n🗞️ We will share the official outcome as soon as it is confirmed.\\n\\n#CollegeSoccer\",\n        \"publishedAt\": \"2026-11-06T08:11:31.000Z\",\n        \"reactionCount\": 2,\n        \"commentCount\": 0,\n        \"isPaidPartnership\": null,\n        \"sharedPostId\": null,\n        \"sharedPostUrl\": null,\n        \"author\": {\n          \"id\": \"100064894560007\",\n          \"name\": \"Sports Recruiting USA\",\n          \"url\": null\n        },\n        \"video\": {\n          \"thumbnailUrl\": null,\n          \"durationMs\": null,\n          \"sdUrl\": null,\n          \"hdUrl\": null\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"3750352965117984\",\n        \"url\": \"https://www.facebook.com/groups/862950587191584/permalink/3750352965117984/\",\n        \"text\": \"🚨 Sources say the “no” vote tally on the NCAA Division I Men’s Soccer Redistribution Model has hit 241\\nThe exact number needed to rescind the proposal.\\n\\nNote:\\nVotes can still be changed until tomorrow (Nov. 6) at 5 p.m., so nothing is official until the deadline closes.\\n#CollegeSoccer #NCAA\\nSports Recruiting USA\",\n        \"publishedAt\": \"2026-11-06T00:23:04.000Z\",\n        \"reactionCount\": 0,\n        \"commentCount\": 0,\n        \"isPaidPartnership\": null,\n        \"sharedPostId\": null,\n        \"sharedPostUrl\": null,\n        \"author\": {\n          \"id\": \"100001379658890\",\n          \"name\": \"Don Williams\",\n          \"url\": null\n        },\n        \"video\": {\n          \"thumbnailUrl\": null,\n          \"durationMs\": null,\n          \"sdUrl\": null,\n          \"hdUrl\": null\n        }\n      }\n    ],\n    \"page\": {\n      \"nextCursor\": \"AQHT9ClCaEQkTSL6i8W-fYfAbMjUIKs3kQ3kRxDj0XAOfpsTgeFX-WIS5jquqXmlr-TRwh2i1xEPMm1AaUWa9Jrprw:eyIwIjoxNzkzOTgyMDAyLCIxIjo3NjgyLCIzIjoxLCI0IjoxLCI1IjoyLCI2IjotMSwiNyI6LTEsIjgiOi0xfQ==\",\n      \"hasMore\": true\n    }\n  },\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"requestId\": \"req_73bf2f6f-69a8-4a0c-a145-3b949444c9e8\",\n    \"creditsCharged\": 1,\n    \"version\": \"v1\"\n  }\n}"},{"type":"text","text":"{\"conversation_id\":\"01a1b1a8-f120-7535-b663-d0678ea0f48b\"}"}],"structuredContent":{"data":{"lookupStatus":"found","posts":[{"id":"3750981788388435","url":"https://www.facebook.com/groups/862950587191584/permalink/3750981788388435/","text":"Now just imagine the NAIA decided to change their soccer into the two-semester season...","publishedAt":"2026-11-06T11:13:14.000Z","reactionCount":1,"commentCount":2,"isPaidPartnership":null,"sharedPostId":null,"sharedPostUrl":null,"author":{"id":"200300067","name":"Chris Cousins","url":null},"video":{"thumbnailUrl":null,"durationMs":null,"sdUrl":null,"hdUrl":null}},{"id":"3750963885056892","url":"https://www.facebook.com/groups/862950587191584/permalink/3750963885056892/","text":"⚽ **NCAA men’s soccer two-semester model: the numbers behind the debate**\n\nCollege Soccer HQ’s latest public count reports **241 votes to overturn the proposal**, reaching the required threshold.\n\nHere’s the breakdown:\n\n▪️ **140** came from institutions with men’s soccer.\n▪️ **101** came from institutions without men’s soccer.\n▪️ **58%** of the reported rescission votes therefore came from schools that sponsor the sport.\n▪️ **28 institutions** are listed as publicly backing the model.\n\nThe reported rescission count rose from **183 on November 2 to 241 on November 5**, an increase of 58.\n\nSupporters highlight recovery time, player development and reduced midweek travel. Those seeking rescission raise concerns about staffing, costs, facilities, weather and the impact on other sports.\n\nInstitutional positions do not necessarily reflect the views of every coach or player. Schools without a reported position should not automatically be counted as supporting either side.\n\nThese figures reflect public reporting, rather than an official final NCAA tally. The page states that votes can be withdrawn until voting closes on November 6 at 5pm ET.\n\n🔎 Explore the full breakdown and search by school or conference:\n\n[https://collegesoccerhq.com/resources/two-semester-model](https://collegesoccerhq.com/resources/two-semester-model)\n\n#CollegeSoccer #NCAASoccer #SRUSA","publishedAt":"2026-11-06T10:55:29.000Z","reactionCount":7,"commentCount":4,"isPaidPartnership":null,"sharedPostId":null,"sharedPostUrl":null,"author":{"id":"200300067","name":"Chris Cousins","url":null},"video":{"thumbnailUrl":null,"durationMs":null,"sdUrl":null,"hdUrl":null}},{"id":"3750768275076453","url":"https://www.facebook.com/groups/862950587191584/permalink/3750768275076453/","text":"🚨 𝐓𝐖𝐎-𝐒𝐄𝐌𝐄𝐒𝐓𝐄𝐑 𝐌𝐎𝐃𝐄𝐋 𝐔𝐏𝐃𝐀𝐓𝐄\n\n📋 Reports suggest the #NCAA Division I two-semester model for men’s soccer is set to be rescinded. #SRUSA understands that the 241 votes needed have now been reached, and sources indicate the proposal is unlikely to survive.\n\n⚠️ The result has not been officially confirmed, and voting closes today at 5pm ET.\n\n➡️ What this means if the reports are correct:\n\n▪️ The proposal is defeated and Division I men’s soccer stays on its current fall calendar\n\n▪️ The year-round model would not take effect in 2027-28\n\n▪️ The Cabinet affirmed the proposal on 7th October, but it fell short of the 75 percent needed to avoid the rescission period\n\n🗞️ We will share the official outcome as soon as it is confirmed.\n\n#CollegeSoccer","publishedAt":"2026-11-06T08:11:31.000Z","reactionCount":2,"commentCount":0,"isPaidPartnership":null,"sharedPostId":null,"sharedPostUrl":null,"author":{"id":"100064894560007","name":"Sports Recruiting USA","url":null},"video":{"thumbnailUrl":null,"durationMs":null,"sdUrl":null,"hdUrl":null}},{"id":"3750352965117984","url":"https://www.facebook.com/groups/862950587191584/permalink/3750352965117984/","text":"🚨 Sources say the “no” vote tally on the NCAA Division I Men’s Soccer Redistribution Model has hit 241\nThe exact number needed to rescind the proposal.\n\nNote:\nVotes can still be changed until tomorrow (Nov. 6) at 5 p.m., so nothing is official until the deadline closes.\n#CollegeSoccer #NCAA\nSports Recruiting USA","publishedAt":"2026-11-